Now my brother and my sister have the computer.
It is Diego and Sofía.
"Hi Diego and Sofía," I say.
"Hi Maya," says my brother.
"Is your city cold?" he asks.
"Is Denmark a cold country?" my sister asks.
I smile at my family.
"Yes, it is very cold here," I say.
I take my computer.
I walk over to a window.
"Look at my window," I say.
I show them my city.
"Out there is a dark street," I say.
It is evening in Denmark.
"Do you have a good jacket?" Diego asks.
"No, my jacket is too thin," I answer.
Sofía laughs a little.
"But my room is warm," I say.
We talk together for a long time.
